5,Zorop language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/zorop_language,"Zorop, also known as Yafi, is an endangered Eastern Pauwasi language spoken by a small indigenous community in West Papua, Indonesia. [1][2] It is primarily used as a first language by adults in four villages—Yafi, Sungwar-Tainda, Tokondo, and Abiu—in the Warlef village area of Senggi District, Keerom Regency, with no evidence of transmission to children or institutional support beyond the ...",Zorop,Pauwasi
6,East Pauwasi languages — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/east_pauwasi_languages,"The East Pauwasi languages form a small branch of the Pauwasi family within the Papuan languages of New Guinea, consisting of three closely related but underdocumented tongues spoken by small communities in the rugged border highlands between Indonesia and Papua New Guinea. [1] These languages—Emem and Zorop (also known as Yafi) in Indonesian Papua, and Karkar-Yuri in Sandaun Province, Papua ...",Zorop,Pauwasi
